    "summary": "Kente cloth, a rectangular man’s wrapper composed of 23 hand-woven narrow strips of blue and white imported European cotton, hand-sewn together along the selvedges. All the strips have the same continuous design along the entire length; there is no variant pattern at the ends. The warp design consists of white cotton, along which run two sets of triple lines of blue cotton. The weft pattern is also formed of triple lines of blue regularly spaced against a white background. The ends have been hemmed.",
